This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

   The user's single explicit request: "Migrate every route and file from the Pages Router to the App Router. When finished, remove the pages dir entirely. Ensure the proper App Router APIs are used. If a Pages Router API was used that no longer exists in App Router, replace it with the newer version or the new pattern. Make sure to add types."

   Project instructions (CLAUDE.md → AGENTS.md) that constrain how the work must be done, verbatim: "# This is NOT the Next.js you know — This version has breaking changes — APIs, conventions, and file structure may all differ from your training data. Read the relevant guide in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing any code. Heed deprecation notices."

   Session-level constraints from the system prompt: "Do not call the AgentTool unless the user requested it. Do not use workflows or deep-research unless the user requested it." (Both were honored — no subagents/workflows used.)

   No security-sensitive instructions, credential rules, or forbidden-file constraints were stated by the user beyond the above.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Next.js 16.4.0-canary.8 App Router (Turbopack default), React 19.1, TypeScript strict
   - Async Request APIs (v16 breaking): `await params`, `await searchParams`, `await headers()`, `await cookies()`
   - Global typed helpers generated by `next typegen`: `PageProps<'/route'>`, `LayoutProps<'/route'>`, `RouteContext<'/route'>`
   - Root layout replaces `_app.js` + `_document.js`; must define `<html>`/`<body>`; no manual `<head>` tags
   - Metadata API (`export const metadata: Metadata`, `generateMetadata`) replaces `next/head`; `title.template`/`title.default`/`title.absolute`
   - Critical nuance: a layout's `title.template` does NOT apply to a `page` in the same route segment
   - `not-found.js` replaces `pages/404.js`; metadata export IS honored (verified in `lib/metadata/resolve-metadata.js`, errorConvention path)
   - `error.js` + `global-error.js` replace `pages/_error.js`; props are `{ error, retry }` — `retry` stable since v16.3 (`reset` discouraged); error boundaries must be `'use client'`; `global-error` must render its own `<html>/<body>` and import global styles; metadata unsupported in it (use React `<title>`)
   - `route.js` Route Handlers replace `pages/api/*`; Web `Request`/`Response`; unexported methods auto-return 405 + `Allow` header
   - Data fetching: `getServerSideProps` → uncached `fetch(..., { cache: 'no-store' })` + `headers()`; `getStaticProps` + revalidate → `fetch(..., { next: { revalidate: N } })`; `getStaticPaths` → `generateStaticParams`; `fallback: 'blocking'` → `dynamicParams = true`; `notFound: true` → `notFound()` from `next/navigation`
   - fetch is NOT cached by default in v16 (the v13-era migration doc text is outdated)
   - `useRouter` from `next/navigation` (no `isFallback`, `query`, `pathname`, `asPath`); `router.back()`/`push()` still exist
   - `next/font/google` self-hosting replaces `<link>` to Google Fonts (CSS inlining "does not work in app")
   - Streaming vs status codes: with a `loading.tsx`/Suspense fallback, a `notFound()` yields HTTP 200 + `<meta name="robots" content="noindex">`; a real 404 requires no streaming before the check

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **Deleted (via `git rm -r`)**: `pages/404.js`, `pages/_app.js`, `pages/_document.js`, `pages/_error.js`, `pages/index.js`, `pages/blog/index.js`, `pages/blog/[id].js`, `pages/api/posts/index.js`, `pages/api/posts/[id].js`, `components/AppProvider.js`. The `pages/` directory no longer exists.

   - **`lib/posts.ts`** (new) — centralizes typed data access + caching semantics so pages and `generateMetadata` share fetchers (fetch memoization dedupes):
     ```ts
     const API_BASE = 'https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com'
     export interface Post { id: number; userId: number; title: string; body: string }
     export interface PostComment { id: number; postId: number; name: string; email: string; body: string }
     // getRecentPosts(limit = 5): cache: 'no-store'  (was getServerSideProps)
     // getPosts(): next: { revalidate: 60 }          (was getStaticProps + revalidate 60)
     // getPost(id): next: { revalidate: 300 }, returns Post | null
     //   const post: Partial<Post> = await res.json()
     //   return typeof post.id === 'number' ? (post as Post) : null
     // getPostComments(id): next: { revalidate: 300 }, returns [] on !res.ok
     ```

   - **`components/AppProvider.tsx`** (new, replaces .js) — `'use client'`, typed context:
     ```tsx
     export type Theme = 'light' | 'dark'
     export interface AppContextValue { theme: Theme; setTheme: Dispatch<SetStateAction<Theme>> }
     const AppContext = createContext<AppContextValue | null>(null)
     export function AppProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) { const [theme, setTheme] = useState<Theme>('light') ... }
     export function useAppContext(): AppContextValue { ...throws if null... }
     ```

   - **`app/layout.tsx`** (new; replaces `_app.js` + `_document.js`):
     ```tsx
     const inter = Inter({ subsets: ['latin'], weight: ['400','500','600'], display: 'swap', variable: '--font-inter' })
     export const metadata: Metadata = {
       title: { default: 'My Blog', template: '%s - My Blog' },
       description: 'A complex blog application',
       icons: { icon: '/favicon.ico' },
     }
     export default function RootLayout({ children }: LayoutProps<'/'>) {
       return (<html lang="en" className={inter.variable}><body><AppProvider><div className="app-container">
         <header><h1>My Blog</h1><nav><Link href="/">Home</Link><Link href="/blog">Blog</Link></nav></header>
         <main>{children}</main><footer><p>&copy; 2024 My Blog</p></footer>
       </div></AppProvider></body></html>)
     }
     ```

   - **`app/page.tsx`** (new; was `pages/index.js` + getServerSideProps):
     ```tsx
     export const metadata: Metadata = {
       // A `title.template` from a layout does not apply to a page in the same route
       // segment, so the root layout's `%s - My Blog` suffix is spelled out here.
       title: 'Home - My Blog',
       description: 'Welcome to my blog homepage',
       openGraph: { title: 'Home - My Blog' },
     }
     export default async function HomePage() {
       const requestHeaders = await headers()
       const userAgent = requestHeaders.get('user-agent') ?? ''
       const posts = await getRecentPosts()
       const timestamp = new Date().toISOString()
       ... <Link href={`/blog/${post.id}`}> ... <ViewAllPostsButton />
